Shell Scripting Basics
-----------------------
1. First Program
File Name--hello.sh
echo 'This is my first shell script'
Output
This is my first shell script
Learning
echo--display output on screen
2. Variables
File Name--variables.sh
name='velmurali'
age=28
city='chennai'
echo $name
echo $age
echo $city
Output
velmurali
28
chennai
Learning
variable--store value
$--access variable value
3. Variables Inside String
File Name--variables_msg.sh
name='velmurali'
echo "My name is $name"
Output
My name is velmurali
Learning
double quotes expand variables
4. Single vs Double Quotes
File Name--quotes.sh
name='velmurali'
echo '$name'
echo "$name"
Output
$name
velmurali
Learning
single quotes--literal text
double quotes--expand variables
5. User Input
File Name--read_name.sh
echo "Enter Name"
read name
echo "Name is $name"
Output
Enter Name
Velmurali
Name is Velmurali
Learning
read--accept user input
6. IF Condition
File Name--if_age.sh
read age
if [ $age -ge 18 ]
then
echo "Eligible"
fi
Output
20
Eligible
Learning
if--start condition
then--execute block
fi--end condition
7. IF ELSE
File Name--if_else_age.sh
read age
if [ $age -ge 18 ]
then
echo "Eligible"
else
echo "Not Eligible"
fi
Output
17
Not Eligible
Learning
else--execute when condition is false
8. ELIF
File Name--if_marks.sh
read marks
if [ $marks -gt 100 ]
then
echo "Invalid"
elif [ $marks -ge 85 ]
then
echo "Grade A"
elif [ $marks -ge 60 ]
then
echo "Grade B"
else
echo "Grade C"
fi
Output
85
Grade A
Learning
elif--else if condition
9. Logical AND
File Name--and_condition.sh
read age
if [ $age -ge 18 ] && [ $age -le 60 ]
then
echo "Eligible"
fi
Learning
&&--AND operator
10. Logical OR
File Name--or_condition.sh
read marks
if [ $marks -lt 0 ] || [ $marks -gt 100 ]
then
echo "Invalid Marks"
fi
Learning
||--OR operator
11. For Loop
File Name--for_loop.sh
for i in 1 2 3 4 5
do
echo $i
done
Output
1
2
3
4
5
Learning
for--loop through values
do--start loop block
done--end loop block
12. For Loop With Names
File Name--for_names.sh
for name in raj velmurali kumar
do
echo $name
done
Output
raj
velmurali
kumar
Learning
for loop can iterate strings
13. While Loop
File Name--while_loop.sh
count=1
while [ $count -le 5 ]
do
echo $count
count=$((count+1))
done
Output
1
2
3
4
5
Learning
while--execute until condition becomes false
$(( ))--perform arithmetic
14. Case Statement
File Name--case_grade.sh
read grade
case $grade in
A)
echo "Excellent"
;;
B)
echo "Good"
;;
C)
echo "Average"
;;
*)
echo "Invalid Grade"
;;
esac
Output
A
Excellent
Learning
case--multiple conditions
esac--end case block
15. Positional Parameters
File Name--params.sh
echo $1
echo $2
Execution
sh params.sh velmurali chennai
Output
velmurali
chennai
Learning
$1--first argument
$2--second argument
16. Function
File Name--function.sh
greet()
{
echo "Hello Velmurali"
}
greet
Output
Hello Velmurali
Learning
function--reusable block of code
17. Function With Parameters
File Name--function_param.sh
greet()
{
echo "Hello $1"
}
greet Velmurali
Output
Hello Velmurali
Learning
function can accept parameters
18. Exit Status
File Name--exit_status.sh
ls customer.txt
echo $?
Output
0
Learning
$?--status of previous command
0--success
non-zero--failure
19. Call One Script From Another
File Name--main.sh
sh hello.sh
echo "Main Script Completed"
Learning
one script can call another script
20. Current Date In Script
File Name--date_script.sh
echo $(date)
Output
current date and time
Learning
$( )--command substitution
21. Read File Line By Line
File Name--read_file.sh
while read line
do
echo $line
done < customer.txt
Learning
process file record by record

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Realtime
---------
1. Record Count Script
File Name--record_count.sh
echo "Enter File Name"
read file
count=$(wc -l < $file)
echo "Total Records: $count"
Learning
Count records in a file
2. ACTIVE Customer Count
File Name--active_count.sh
count=$(grep -c "|ACTIVE|" customer.txt)
echo "ACTIVE Customers: $count"
Learning
Count ACTIVE records
3. Duplicate Record Check
File Name--duplicate_check.sh
dup_count=$(sort customer.txt | uniq -d | wc -l)
echo "Duplicate Records: $dup_count"
Learning
Identify duplicate records
4. Null Record Check
File Name--null_check.sh
null_count=$(grep -c "||" customer.txt)
echo "Null Records: $null_count"
Learning
Find records with missing values
5. Customer Search Script
File Name--customer_search.sh
echo "Enter Customer ID"
read custid
grep "$custid" customer.txt
Learning
Search specific customer
6. Invalid Balance Check
File Name--negative_balance.sh
awk -F'|' '$5<0' customer.txt
Learning
Find negative balances
7. Zero Balance Check
File Name--zero_balance.sh
awk -F'|' '$5==0' customer.txt
Learning
Find zero balance customers
8. Total Balance Calculation
File Name--total_balance.sh
awk -F'|' 'NR>1 {sum+=$5} END{print sum}' customer.txt
Learning
Calculate total balance
9. Customer Status Report
File Name--status_report.sh
echo "ACTIVE : $(grep -c "|ACTIVE|" customer.txt)"
echo "INACTIVE : $(grep -c "|INACTIVE|" customer.txt)"
echo "CLOSED : $(grep -c "|CLOSED|" customer.txt)"
Learning
Generate status summary
10. File Validation Script
File Name--file_validation.sh
echo "Total Records : $(wc -l < customer.txt)"
echo "Duplicate Records : $(sort customer.txt | uniq -d | wc -l)"
echo "Null Records : $(grep -c "||" customer.txt)"
Learning
Basic batch file validation
11. Log Error Count
File Name--error_count.sh
grep -c "ERROR" app.log
Learning
Count application errors
12. Log Error Extraction
File Name--error_extract.sh
grep "ERROR" app.log > error.log
Learning
Separate error records
13. Find Large Directories
File Name--disk_usage.sh
du -sh *
Learning
Find space consuming folders
14. Disk Space Check
File Name--disk_check.sh
df -h
Learning
Verify filesystem space
15. Batch Health Check Script
File Name--health_check.sh
echo "Record Count : $(wc -l < customer.txt)"
echo "Duplicate Count : $(sort customer.txt | uniq -d | wc -l)"
echo "Null Count : $(grep -c "||" customer.txt)"
echo "ACTIVE Count : $(grep -c "|ACTIVE|" customer.txt)"
Learning
Daily support validation script
